If a patient has a subacute-pain and starts an opioid-therapy for an acute-pain and receives the opioid-therapy during at least 30 days then every clinician should conduct a follow-up with the patient and should evaluate the patient and should reassess the subacute-pain for the patient and should reassess a patient-function for the patient and should reassess a treatment-course for the patient and should prevent an unintentional-long-term-opioid-therapy-initiation for the patient.
If a patient has a subacute-pain and starts an opioid-therapy for an acute-pain and receives the opioid-therapy during at least 30 days and the patient has a potentially-reversible-chronic-pain-cause then every clinician should address the potentially-reversible-chronic-pain-cause for the patient.
